      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about glitches but it feels too coordinated. like if it was just a bug it would be random, but it feels aimed. and i've read some theories online about \"sub-audible frequencies\" being used to transmit data through light pulses or even through the haptic feedback of devices. if a company wanted to harvest data on what people say in their homes without anyone knowing, wouldn't they hide it inside the standard telemetry or \"diagnostic\" data the devices already send back to the cloud? it almost seems more efficient than trying to hack a phone.",
